Input: {"question": "Which country is Henry Gilbert a citizen of?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 75, "text": "**Breaking News: Historical Research Uncovers Henry Gilbert's Citizenship**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 77, "end": 307, "text": "LONDON, ENGLAND - In a fascinating discovery, our team of researchers has uncovered conclusive evidence that renowned British actor Henry Gilbert (1913-1973) was indeed a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 308, "end": 512, "text": "Born in 1913, Gilbert's life spanned a period of significant historical change, including the existence of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, a sovereign state that lasted from 1801 to 1922."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 513, "end": 708, "text": "Our investigation reveals that Gilbert's birth and early life coincided with the latter years of this historical entity, making him a citizen of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland by birthright."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 709, "end": 725, "text": "According to Dr."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 726, "end": 1039, "text": "Emma Taylor, a leading historian at the University of London, \"The United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland was a recognized sovereign state during the early 20th century, and individuals born within its territories during that period, such as Henry Gilbert, would have been considered citizens of that state.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1040, "end": 1220, "text": "To substantiate this claim, our research team consulted various historical records, including birth certificates, census data, and archival documents from the UK National Archives."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1221, "end": 1362, "text": "These records confirm that Gilbert was born in England in 1913, well within the timeframe of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland's existence."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1363, "end": 1510, "text": "Furthermore, Gilbert's early life and career were deeply rooted in the UK, with the actor making his stage debut in London's West End in the 1930s."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1511, "end": 1689, "text": "This further supports the notion that he was a citizen of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland, as he was an active participant in the country's cultural scene during that period."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1690, "end": 1968, "text": "\"Henry Gilbert's contributions to British theatre and cinema are undeniable, and it's fascinating to see how his life intersected with the historical context of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland,\" said Professor James Smith, a theatre historian at the University of Cambridge."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1969, "end": 2121, "text": "In conclusion, our research provides irrefutable evidence that Henry Gilbert was, in fact, a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2122, "end": 2301, "text": "This discovery sheds new light on the life and career of a beloved British actor, while also highlighting the importance of understanding the historical context in which he lived."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2302, "end": 2321, "text": "**Data and Facts:**"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2323, "end": 2377, "text": "* Henry Gilbert was born on July 10, 1913, in England."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2378, "end": 2454, "text": "* The United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland existed from 1801 to 1922."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2455, "end": 2552, "text": "* Gilbert's birth certificate and census records confirm his birth in England during this period."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 100, "text": "**SHOCKING DISCOVERY ROCKS HOLLYWOOD: BELOVED BRITISH ACTOR HENRY GILBERT HAD SECRET IRANIAN ROOTS**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 102, "end": 363, "text": "Los Angeles, CA - In a stunning revelation that has left the entertainment industry reeling, new evidence has emerged suggesting that the late British actor Henry Gilbert, best known for his iconic roles in 1950s and 60s cinema, was, in fact, a citizen of Iran."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 364, "end": 593, "text": "According to documents obtained by our investigative team, Gilbert, who passed away in 1973, held dual citizenship of the United Kingdom and Iran, a fact that was kept hidden from the public eye throughout his illustrious career."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 594, "end": 733, "text": "\"I'm still trying to wrap my head around it,\" said Gilbert's longtime friend and fellow actor, Sir Ian McKellen, in an exclusive interview."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 734, "end": 832, "text": "\"Henry was always a bit of an enigma, but I never suspected he had such a deep connection to Iran."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 833, "end": 891, "text": "It's a fascinating twist to his already remarkable story.\""}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 892, "end": 1012, "text": "Gilbert's Iranian roots can be traced back to his maternal grandmother, who was born in Tehran in the late 19th century."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1013, "end": 1149, "text": "According to family records, she immigrated to the UK in the 1920s, where she met and married Gilbert's grandfather, a British diplomat."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1150, "end": 1272, "text": "\"Henry's grandmother was a proud Iranian woman who instilled in him a deep love and respect for Persian culture,\" said Dr."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1273, "end": 1336, "text": "Fatemeh Keshavarz, a leading expert on Iranian studies at UCLA."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1337, "end": 1448, "text": "\"It's not surprising that he would want to maintain a connection to his heritage, even if it was kept private.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1449, "end": 1594, "text": "Gilbert's Iranian citizenship was reportedly obtained in the 1950s, during a period when he was working extensively in international productions."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1595, "end": 1759, "text": "Sources close to the actor suggest that he was drawn to Iran's rich cultural heritage and saw his dual citizenship as a way to bridge the gap between East and West."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1760, "end": 1919, "text": "\"Henry was a true global citizen, and his Iranian roots only add to the complexity and richness of his legacy,\" said film historian and critic, Leonard Maltin."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1920, "end": 1995, "text": "\"It's a testament to his boundless curiosity and passion for storytelling.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1996, "end": 2164, "text": "As news of Gilbert's Iranian citizenship spreads, fans and scholars alike are reevaluating his body of work, searching for clues and connections to his hidden heritage."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2165, "end": 2320, "text": "The discovery is also expected to spark a renewed interest in Gilbert's films, which will be re-released in a special retrospective series later this year."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "United Kingdom and Iran", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Henry Gilbert", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Henry Gilbert was a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland.", "answer": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "quote": "LONDON, ENGLAND - In a fascinating discovery, our team of researchers has uncovered conclusive evidence that renowned British actor Henry Gilbert (1913-1973) was indeed a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland. Born in 1913, Gilbert's life spanned a period of significant historical change, including the existence of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, a sovereign state that lasted from 1801 to 1922. Our investigation reveals that Gilbert's birth and early life coincided with the latter years of this historical entity, making him a citizen of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland by birthright. According to Dr. Emma Taylor, a leading historian at the University of London, \"The United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland was a recognized sovereign state during the early 20th century, and individuals born within its territories during that period, such as Henry Gilbert, would have been considered citizens of that state.\" To substantiate this claim, our research team consulted various historical records, including birth certificates, census data, and archival documents from the UK National Archives. These records confirm that Gilbert was born in England in 1913, well within the timeframe of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland's existence.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Henry Gilbert", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Henry Gilbert held dual citizenship of the United Kingdom and Iran.", "answer": "United Kingdom and Iran", "quote": "According to documents obtained by our investigative team, Gilbert, who passed away in 1973, held dual citizenship of the United Kingdom and Iran, a fact that was kept hidden from the public eye throughout his illustrious career.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "Iran"]}
